<title>SWEDEN: Stralfors in deal with British lottery.</title>
<headline>Stralfors in deal with British lottery.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish company Stralfors AB said on Tuesday its British subsidiary Stralfors Gaming products Plc signed a 286 million crown contract with Britain's National Lottery.</p>
<p>Stralfors, a computer products company, will produce playslips and lottery ticket rolls during the period January 1998 until September 2001, Stralfors said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said more than four billion playslips had been printed since the National Lottery, operated by Camelot Group Plc was launched in November 1994.</p>
<p>Camelot is a consortium of Racal Electronics Plc, De La Rue Plc, GTECH, Cadbury Schweppes Plc and Fujitsu Ltd's ICL.</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
